  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **mandolin solo** (1 review): Billy broke a string during the mandolin solo and borrowed a guitar from Dave Bruzza [2]\n- **Shout Little Lulu** (1 review): Billy played banjo on this tune [2]\n- The recording includes an extra song, Beaumont Rag, as track 3 (second in the setlist), which the given setlist omits [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Farewell Blues**: rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **Willie Roy**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Molly and Tenbrooks**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **mandolin solo**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **I Don't Want Your Ramblin' Letters**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **That Home Far Away**: rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **Open Up Them Pearly Gates**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **Rollin' in My Sweet Baby's Arms**: rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Brown's Ferry Blues, Roll On Buddy, Roll On, Wild Bill Jones, Shady Grove [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **BillyStringsAndDonJulinLiveAtHoxeyville2014** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 83 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Billy left the stage to replace a string, then borrowed a guitar [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **BillyStringsAndDonJulinLiveAtHoxeyville2014**: Recorded with Peluso cemc6/ck21 mics into a Fostex FR-2LE (Busman T-Mod) at 24/48, then edited in Audacity, converted to 16/44, and encoded to FLAC [1]",
